{
  "id": "GA-SB-319-2022",
  "scope": "state:ga",
  "title": "SB 319 (Chairman John Meadows Act, as signed; Act 596; also called Georgia Constitutional Carry Act of 2021) (2021-2022 session (2022 Regular)) — Ends the license requirement to carry a handgun for people eligible for a license; term \"lawful weapons carrier\"",
  "urls": [
    "https://law-journals-books.vlex.com/vid/sb-319-chairman-john-935400390",
    "https://www.legis.ga.gov/api/document/docs/default-source/house-budget-and-research-office-document-library/newsandhighlights/2022/2022_policy_brief_constitutional_carry.pdf?sfvrsn=194fdfde_2",
    "https://legiscan.com/GA/votes/SB319/2021 (listed by search, not opened: Cloudflare 403 on the LegiScan bill page)",
    "https://www.legis.ga.gov/legislation/60797",
    "https://www.legis.ga.gov/api/legislation/document/20212022/211518 (enrolled text, via LegiScan getBillText doc 2563270)"
  ],
  "version": "enrolled",
  "operative_text": "Enrolled SB 319 (AP), read from the LegiScan copy of the official PDF (https://www.legis.ga.gov/api/legislation/document/20212022/211518); the PDF prints struck and inserted words together; the enacted reading is given.\nSec. 2, OCGA 16-11-125.1(2.1): 'Lawful weapons carrier' means any person who is licensed or eligible for a license pursuant to Code Section 16-11-129 and who is not otherwise prohibited by law from possessing or carrying a weapon.\nSec. 4, OCGA 16-11-126(g)(1): Except as otherwise provided in subsections (a) through (f) of this Code section, no person shall carry a weapon unless he or she is a lawful weapons carrier.",
